# HOUSE CONSTRUCTION PROJECT — FULL CONTEXT FOR CONTINUATION (v4)

## PROJECT OVERVIEW
- **Location:** Bhagamandala–Talakaveri Road (on a CURVE), Kodagu, Karnataka
- **3 km from Talakaveri temple**, left side when traveling to temple
- **Coffee plantation** below (west), road on east. **Isolated, no neighbors.**
- **Plot:** 60 ft (E-W) × 50 ft (N-S), East-facing, highway on East
- **Building:** G+1, 42 ft (N-S) × 38 ft (E-W) total (incl. 8 ft veranda)
- **Style:** Traditional Kodagu with Mangalore tile hip roof, laterite walls
- **Budget:** ~₹1 Crore (v4 all-inclusive)
- **Version:** v4 — Major layout redesign (April 2026)

## v4 KEY CHANGES FROM v3
1. Building widened: 42×38 (was 40×32) = +490 sqft
2. Bedrooms: FULL RECTANGLES (were L-shaped in v3 due to carved-in baths)
3. Baths: ALL 7×10 = 70 sqft (v3 had 48/35/48 sqft — Bath2 was cramped)
4. Back-to-back bath core: Single plumbing stack (saves ₹30-40K)
5. Kitchen ADJACENT to Store (shared wall with door)
6. FF: Dedicated Work Room 14×10 (140 sqft) — user works remotely for months
7. Sitout: ONE 26×8 (208 sqft) replaces 2 small balconies (156 sqft total)
8. Sitout faces WEST (plantation + hill views), supported by 3 pillars below
9. Comprehensive safety: 7' solid wall (road), CCTV 4 cameras, MS grills ALL windows, motion lights
10. Total: ~2,909 sqft built-up (was ~2,222)

